               4:05  TOTAL time spent

The hardest part of this assignment was dealing with the various bugs that 
come with concurrent programming. Implementing the functionalities was
relatively straightforward, but there are so many new classes of bugs that
come with concurrent code that I took a lot of time debugging failed test
cases. Some of the more annoying bugs were when I forgot to defer closing a
channel or calling Done() on a WaitGroup. It was also challenging dealing with
select statements when I want to prioritize one case over the other, since Go
picks a case to run uniformly at random. I also spent a decent amount of time
refreshing myself on Go as I haven't used it in a while.
